---
title: Containers & grid
description: A handful of layout utilities that cover most arrangements without a breakpoint. They are real Tailwind utilities, so variants work — md:im-grid-auto.
eyebrow: Layout
source: src/utilities/index.css
---
<h2>Containers</h2>
<p><code>im-wrap</code> centres content at a maximum width. The page already has a gutter (<code>.im-shell-main</code>'s padding), so a wrap adds none of its own.</p>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Utility</th><th>Max width</th><th>For</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-wrap-prose</code></td><td>44rem</td><td>Reading: a post body, a doc.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-wrap</code></td><td>72rem</td><td>A page: article plus rail, a landing page. Override with <code>--im-wrap</code>.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-wrap-wide</code></td><td>90rem</td><td>Galleries, feeds.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-bleed</code></td><td>—</td><td>Break out of the gutter to the viewport edges.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>The same widths exist as <code>max-w-prose</code>, <code>max-w-page</code>, <code>max-w-wide</code>.</p>

<h2>im-grid-auto</h2>
<p>As many columns as fit at a minimum width. Set <code>--im-grid-min</code> and <code>--im-grid-gap</code>. This is the workhorse: post feeds, card lists, swatches.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto im-grid-sm">
	<div class="demo-cell">1</div><div class="demo-cell">2</div><div class="demo-cell">3</div><div class="demo-cell">4</div><div class="demo-cell">5</div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>im-grid-fit</h2>
<p>The same, but with few items the columns stretch to fill the row instead of leaving empty tracks.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit im-grid-sm">
	<div class="demo-cell">1</div><div class="demo-cell">2</div><div class="demo-cell">3</div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>The twelve columns</h2>
<p>Every layout in the system is <strong>measured</strong> in one 12-column grid with one gap, <code>--im-grid-gap</code>: a widget rail is four columns (<code>--im-span-4</code>), a contents rail two, a hero's measure seven, a clip's room five, the player's side three. The grid is never drawn on a page — a section fits it by being sized in it. <code>im-cols</code> is the grid itself, for placing things with <code>col-span-*</code>; <code>im-guides</code> draws the columns inside one container while you build, and comes out again.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-cols" style="position: relative">
	<span class="im-guides" aria-hidden="true"></span>
	<div class="col-span-8 im-ring-line rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-muted bg-canvas">col-span-8 — an article</div>
	<div class="col-span-4 im-ring-line rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-muted bg-canvas">col-span-4 — its rail</div>
	<div class="col-span-7 im-ring-line rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-muted bg-canvas">7 — a hero's measure</div>
	<div class="col-span-5 im-ring-line rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-muted bg-canvas">5 — a clip's room</div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<div class="im-table-scroll"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Is</th><th>Used by</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>--im-col</code></td><td>one column of the box it is read in</td><td>everything below</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-span-2</code></td><td>two columns and a gap</td><td><code>im-with-rails</code>' contents rail</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-span-3</code></td><td>three</td><td><code>im-with-aside</code>, <code>im-single-aside-sm</code>, the player's side</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-span-4</code></td><td>four</td><td><code>im-single</code>, <code>im-with-aside-wide</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-span-5</code></td><td>five</td><td><code>im-shortwatch</code>'s clip</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-span-7</code></td><td>seven</td><td><code>im-collhero</code>'s words</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Under 48rem it is four columns, which is what a phone can hold.</p>

<h2>im-grid-page</h2>
<p>Twelve columns, for a deliberate composition. Place children with Tailwind's <code>col-span-*</code>, responsive as usual.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-page">
	<div class="demo-cell col-span-12 md:col-span-8">col-span-12 md:col-span-8</div>
	<div class="demo-cell col-span-12 md:col-span-4">md:col-span-4</div>
	<div class="demo-cell col-span-6 md:col-span-3">3</div><div class="demo-cell col-span-6 md:col-span-3">3</div><div class="demo-cell col-span-12 md:col-span-6">6</div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>im-cluster &amp; im-stack</h2>
<p><code>im-cluster</code> is a wrapping row (<code>--im-cluster-gap</code>); <code>im-stack</code> is a column (<code>--im-stack-gap</code>, default one line of rhythm).</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-stack">
	<div class="im-cluster"><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-btn-primary" href="#cluster-stack">Save</a><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm" href="#cluster-stack">Cancel</a><span class="im-badge im-badge-warning">Unsaved</span></div>
	<div class="im-cluster"><a class="im-tag" href="#cluster-stack">Travel</a><a class="im-tag" href="#cluster-stack">Craft</a><a class="im-tag" href="#cluster-stack">Career</a></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>im-ring-line</h2>
<p>A 1px border drawn as an inset shadow: it takes no space, and being translucent it works on any surface. Use it wherever you would reach for <code>border</code>.</p>
{{#example center=true}}
<div class="im-ring-line rounded-xl px-5 py-4 text-sm">ring-line</div>
<div class="im-ring-line bg-surface rounded-xl px-5 py-4 text-sm">on a surface</div>
{{/example}}
